WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:15.701
Mr. Pendleton's house looked quite different from the last time Pollyanna was there.

2
00:00:17.562 --> 00:00:20.544
Every window was open, and the doctor's carriage was outside.

3
00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:27.089
Leaving her stew in the kitchen, Pollyanna followed a maid down the hall.

4
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.271
They passed Dr.

5
00:00:30.291 --> 00:00:32.945
Chilton and a male nurse, who was surprised Dr.

6
00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:34.366
Chilton was permitting a visitor.

7
00:00:34.386 --> 00:00:37.808
"I thought Mr.

8
00:00:37.828 --> 00:00:40.810
Pendleton didn't want visitors," the nurse said to Dr.

9
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.953
Chilton. "If anyone can improve his mood, it's that child."

10
00:00:46.494 --> 00:00:47.154
"Who is she?"

11
00:00:48.675 --> 00:00:49.816
The doctor hesitated.

12
00:00:49.836 --> 00:00:54.579
"Pollyanna Whittier is the niece of a prominent Beldingsville resident.

13
00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.562
I don't know Pollyanna well, but many of my patients do.

14
00:00:59.643 --> 00:01:01.524
She does them more good than some medicines!"

15
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:03.761
The nurse smiled.

16
00:01:03.781 --> 00:01:05.923
"What's her secret ingredient?"

17
00:01:05.943 --> 00:01:10.026
"An overwhelming gladness about everything.

18
00:01:11.287 --> 00:01:14.370
I wish I could prescribe her to all my patients," Dr.

19
00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:15.170
Chilton joked.

20
00:01:17.232 --> 00:01:22.296
Meanwhile, as Pollyanna and the maid passed the library, Pollyanna noticed how clean it was.

21
00:01:25.278 --> 00:01:28.081
The maid opened a door, and Pollyanna entered a room.

22
00:01:29.382 --> 00:01:31.764
Mr. Pendleton was inside, lying in bed.

23
00:01:33.152 --> 00:01:34.713
"I said I didn't want—," Mr.

24
00:01:34.753 --> 00:01:36.793
Pendleton began in an angry voice.

25
00:01:36.813 --> 00:01:38.694
"Oh, it's you!"

26
00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:42.015
He almost smiled when he spotted Pollyanna.

27
00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:45.155
"I'm so glad to see you!"

28
00:01:46.536 --> 00:01:48.136
Pollyanna rushed to his side.

29
00:01:48.156 --> 00:01:52.497
"Well, I'm not glad to be stuck in bed with a broken leg."

30
00:01:54.598 --> 00:01:57.159
"At least you can be glad you didn't break both legs."

31
00:01:57.179 --> 00:02:01.900
"Yes, I'm lucky," the man said sarcastically.

32
00:02:03.016 --> 00:02:08.398
"I should be glad I'm not a centipede with a hundred broken legs."

33
00:02:08.418 --> 00:02:09.499
"Oh, that's a good one!"

34
00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:12.220
Pollyanna laughed, and Mr.

35
00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.901
Pendleton found himself smiling despite himself.

36
00:02:16.141 --> 00:02:17.822
But his mood soon soured again.

37
00:02:17.842 --> 00:02:22.804
"I hate having all these people in my house and needing to pay them too!"

38
00:02:22.824 --> 00:02:28.046
"Yes, Nancy told me you don't like spending money.

39
00:02:29.347 --> 00:02:31.668
I guess you're saving it for orphans overseas."

40
00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:33.928
"What are you talking about?

41
00:02:34.068 --> 00:02:34.729
Who's Nancy?"

42
00:02:36.309 --> 00:02:38.450
"Nancy works for my aunt, Polly Harrington.

43
00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.731
After my father died, Aunt Polly took me in.

44
00:02:42.731 --> 00:02:44.291
My mother was her sister Jennie."

45
00:02:48.072 --> 00:02:50.393
Mr. Pendleton groaned and closed his eyes.

46
00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:54.034
He looked so upset that Pollyanna was frightened.

47
00:02:54.054 --> 00:02:58.055
"Maybe I should go now," she said.

48
00:02:58.075 --> 00:03:00.216
"Enjoy the stew I've brought!"

49
00:03:03.904 --> 00:03:05.525
"Wait!" Mr.

50
00:03:05.565 --> 00:03:08.446
Pendleton opened his eyes and gazed fondly at Pollyanna.

51
00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:11.887
"So, you're Miss Polly's niece.

52
00:03:13.068 --> 00:03:14.508
I can't believe she sent me stew."

53
00:03:16.689 --> 00:03:17.650
"Oh, no, sir!"

54
00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.310
Pollyanna said with alarm.

55
00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:23.412
"She said I must be sure not to let you think that."

56
00:03:23.432 --> 00:03:25.313
"Never mind!"

57
00:03:25.693 --> 00:03:27.233
the man snapped and turned away.

58
00:03:29.174 --> 00:03:31.435
Pollyanna tiptoed from the room and found Dr.

59
00:03:31.475 --> 00:03:33.396
Chilton waiting to offer her a ride home.

60
00:03:36.428 --> 00:03:37.909
"I love to ride!"

61
00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.492
Pollyanna beamed at the doctor as they drove away.

62
00:03:41.512 --> 00:03:45.455
"From what I've heard, you love most things."

63
00:03:47.677 --> 00:03:48.638
Pollyanna laughed.

64
00:03:49.138 --> 00:03:51.981
"That's true, but mostly I love just living.

65
00:03:53.362 --> 00:03:57.085
Of course, Aunt Polly says my days must also be profitable."

66
00:03:57.105 --> 00:04:00.247
"That sounds like something she'd say."

67
00:04:01.588 --> 00:04:05.952
Dr. Chilton looked so sad that Pollyanna wished she could do something for him.

68
00:04:07.532 --> 00:04:10.293
They rode in silence until Pollyanna was almost home.

69
00:04:10.313 --> 00:04:18.077
"Dr. Chilton," Pollyanna finally said, "I think you're in the gladdest business of all."

70
00:04:19.537 --> 00:04:21.158
The doctor turned to her in surprise.

71
00:04:21.178 --> 00:04:25.460
"How can you say that when I see so many people suffering every day?"

72
00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:29.662
"Because you're helping them, and you're glad to help them.

73
00:04:30.882 --> 00:04:34.104
So that makes you the gladdest person in Beldingsville."

74
00:04:36.268 --> 00:04:39.489
Dr. Chilton looked away as his eyes filled with tears.

75
00:04:40.729 --> 00:04:44.070
He led a lonely life with no wife and no real home.

76
00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:48.092
He lived in his two-room office in a boardinghouse.

77
00:04:50.832 --> 00:04:53.493
But this little girl had made him appreciate his work.

78
00:04:54.833 --> 00:04:56.274
"Thank you for saying that, Pollyanna.

79
00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:59.435
Today the doctor needed some of your medicine too."

80
00:04:59.455 --> 00:05:01.856
"My medicine?"

81
00:05:02.156 --> 00:05:03.016
Pollyanna asked.

82
00:05:06.476 --> 00:05:08.698
But they'd arrived at Aunt Polly's, and Dr.

83
00:05:08.738 --> 00:05:11.059
Chilton was suddenly eager to be on his way.

84
00:05:13.001 --> 00:05:15.903
Pollyanna found Aunt Polly looking out the sitting room window.

85
00:05:15.923 --> 00:05:19.826
"Why were you in Dr.

86
00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.047
Chilton's carriage?"

87
00:05:21.467 --> 00:05:22.128
she demanded.

88
00:05:22.148 --> 00:05:25.250
"He offered me a ride home from Mr.

89
00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:29.993
Pendleton's." Pollyanna couldn't understand why Aunt Polly was annoyed.

90
00:05:31.374 --> 00:05:33.176
But Pollyanna could try to cheer her up.

91
00:05:34.604 --> 00:05:35.345
"I told Mr.

92
00:05:35.365 --> 00:05:37.066
Pendleton you didn't send the stew."

93
00:05:38.768 --> 00:05:40.409
Aunt Polly scolded Pollyanna.

94
00:05:40.429 --> 00:05:44.373
"I said you should be sure he didn't think I sent it.

95
00:05:45.314 --> 00:05:48.757
Which is far different from telling him that I didn't send it."

96
00:05:48.777 --> 00:05:56.184
"I don't see any difference," Pollyanna said as she went to hang up her hat.
